---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { journey, patterns } from '../../data/design-lab';
---
<Base
  title="Process | Design Lab | AllemanIT"
  description="How I build sites now: a repo per site, brand tokens in one file, the same parts wired to a new brand each time, and four versions before one ships."
  url="https://allemanit.com/design-lab/process/"
>
  <Fragment slot="head"><link rel="canonical" href="https://allemanit.com/design-lab/process/" /></Fragment>

  <section class="container-x pt-10 pb-6">
    <a href="/design-lab/" class="text-sm text-white/60 hover:text-white">← Design Lab</a>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-extrabold text-white sm:text-5xl">How the sausage gets made</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg text-white/70">Four stops to get here, one token file per brand, and a short list of parts I stopped rebuilding. None of it is clever. All of it is what made the next site take a weekend instead of a month.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- THE STACK JOURNEY -->
  <section class="container-x py-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">How I got here</h2>
    <p class="mt-1 mb-8 text-white/60">Each stop taught me what the next one needed to fix.</p>
    <ol class="relative ml-3 border-l border-white/15">
      {journey.map((j) => (
        <li class="relative mb-8 pl-7 last:mb-0">
          <span class="absolute -left-1.5 top-1 h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-brand-orange"></span>
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-orange">{j.when}</div>
          <div class="mt-0.5 font-bold text-white">{j.what}</div>
          <p class="mt-1 max-w-2xl text-sm text-white/60">{j.lesson}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <!-- BRAND SYSTEM + PATTERNS -->
  <section class="container-x py-10">
    <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="card min-w-0 p-7">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-brand-orange">The brand system</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold text-white">Colors live in one file.</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-white/70 leading-relaxed">Each brand is a token file of HSL triples. A sync script vendors it into every site. Components only ever say <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">bg-primary</code> or <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">text-accent</code>, never a hex value. Change the orange once, every site follows on the next push.</p>
        <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-black/40 p-4 text-xs text-white/80"><code>:root &#123;
  --primary: 24 100% 50%;   /* the orange */
  --accent:  210 100% 50%;
  --background: 0 0% 100%;
&#125;
/* components */
.btn &#123; background: hsl(var(--primary)); &#125;
.card &#123; background: hsl(var(--primary) / 0.08); &#125;</code></pre>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-white/50">HSL, not OKLCH, on purpose: the <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1 text-xs">hsl(var(--x) / 0.1)</code> opacity form is load-bearing in Tailwind and OKLCH breaks it for zero gain.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card min-w-0 p-7">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-brand-orange">Patterns I stopped rebuilding</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold text-white">The same pieces, every time.</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-white/70 leading-relaxed">After enough sites the parts repeat. These are templates now, and a new site is mostly wiring them to a brand.</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
          {patterns.map((p) => (<li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm text-white/75"><span class="mt-1 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-orange"></span>{p}</li>))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW A SITE GETS MADE -->
  <section class="container-x py-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">A site, start to finish</h2>
    <p class="mt-1 mb-6 max-w-3xl text-white/60">The loop I actually run. Most of the time goes into the first and last step.</p>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      {[
        { n: '01', t: 'Steal the real content', d: 'Their photos, their prices, their hours, their words off the Facebook page. A mockup with lorem ipsum tells you nothing.' },
        { n: '02', t: 'Three or four directions', d: 'Deliberately different on real axes, not recolors. Pick one, borrow from another, throw the rest in the lab.' },
        { n: '03', t: 'Tokens, then build', d: 'The winner becomes a token file. Components get wired to it. The lightest framework that does the job.' },
        { n: '04', t: 'Repo, push, done', d: 'GitHub to Cloudflare Pages. A push is a deploy. No dashboard, no plugins, nothing to babysit.' },
      ].map((s) => (
        <div class="card p-5">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-brand-orange">{s.n}</div>
          <div class="mt-1 font-bold text-white">{s.t}</div>
          <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-white/65">{s.d}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container-x py-10">
    <div class="card flex flex-col items-start justify-between gap-4 p-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">See the output</h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-white/60">Every site this process produced, and the versions it rejected.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/design-lab/sites/" class="btn btn-primary text-sm">The sites</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
